BLOCK ORDER IS NOT COVERED BY THIS GATE. Reordering moves the result
      3.851e-07 (vs the kernel's own 3.473e-07 from the fp32 reference, and the
      1.039e-03 that prefill_attn's bf16-P rounding already costs). Order is a
      bit-exactness question here, not a correctness one.

NOTE: the gap against the bf16-P reference is this kernel being MORE
      accurate, not less. tools/prefill_attn.py rounds P to bf16 because
      tl.dot needs a tensor-core dtype; this kernel's hand-rolled FMA dot
      has no reason to pay that. DO NOT 'fix' the kernel toward the bf16-P
      number -- that makes the port worse to make a number prettier.
      Consequence to expect: being more accurate means DIVERGING from the
      Python engine, and ulp differences flip MoE router decisions. So
      end-to-end validation is on OUTPUT QUALITY, not bit-identity, and a
      per-layer bisect is only valid up to the FIRST routing flip.
